Z||000011||Xtreme Fiero's||10-03-2000||10:22 PM||||You guys should stop laughing @ the imports the Acura Integra Type-R makes 195hp stock from a 1.8L 4cyl that means your 2.8 would make almost 290hp  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> stock to equal the HP to dispalcement ratio of a 1.8 VTEC. i will gladly stop defending the imports when I hear a story of a STOCK!!! GT beating a STOCK Integra Type-R   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> or a 95-99 Eclipse GS-T   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> any one ever beat a 3000GT even a 300zx.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I would LOVE to see ANY fiero beat a Triple rotor wankle powered RX-Z  from Japan or even a Skyline GT-R   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> <BR>and just to let every one know I think the Honda VTEC system cam out before the Northstar  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Xtreme Fiero's (edited 10-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Xtreme Fiero's||10-03-2000||10:25 PM||||I almost forgot let the flames come cause I got a Nissan to!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||Songman||10-03-2000||11:09 PM||||Hey Xtreme.. no offense, but my aunt's 99 Northstar Caddy will outrun her 1972 Caddy too... Of course, factory cars from the 90s will outrun factory cars from the 80s in the same class regardless of what they are...<P>But what I really wanted to say was that I bought a new Grand Am SE back in 90 and it had the HO Quad4. I loved it! Ran it for 140k before some old guy in Nashville decided I was on his part of the street and put me on the sidewalk! If I knew then what I know now, I would have bought that totalled Grand Am from the insurance company and would be riding around with that motor in the little 88 coupe. Someday I'll find another one...||||reg||12
Z||000014||DaRkLoRD||10-04-2000||12:24 AM||||I highly doubt a stock Fiero could ever beat a 3000GT... they're in totally different classes.. A real Type-R is a sports car. not a ricer.. a base model civic with a type-R sticker, is a ricer.<BR>I like acura integras.. and 3000GTs.. and eagle talons.. and mazda RX7s.. and mazda MX3s.. and honda del sols.. I'm pretty sure a fiero could beat an mx3 (he*l I smoked one completely in my mom's ford taurus.. same with a civic.. the guy was revving the cr@p out of it.. hahaha)<P>anyway, there are some d@mn nice import sports cars.. but most of us aren't referring to them when we talk about ricers.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Racer 1||10-04-2000||01:20 AM||||dam-it dont you think the little stickers on the side of the ricer cars are like badges of courage. 4clyd squeeling the front tires like a dragster. theres no way a stock iron duck could take on todays higer powered import engines. But just be proud of the fact you own a  part of history a pontiac fiero.<P>------------------<BR> <P>||||reg||3
Z||000016||HYPTNOTiSE||10-04-2000||03:13 AM||||yeah a type-r integra might make 195hp at 9K rpm, but i bet it only makes like .2 ft pounds of peak torque.  Dude i'm not that impressed by integras, all my buddys have them. None of my close living buddies have fieros.  My one friend who can drive well(so it's not his fault) has a 96 GSR.  jackson supercharger, greddy catback, dc sports intake, underdrive pulleys, and a dc sports stainless header, upgraded fuel pump etc. and he's running 14.0's. Ok with about 5K in mods and only running 14.0's! I'll pass. Hey i guess i'm just another cheap fiero owner. I've driven a 97 3000GT vr-4, acutally i should say i ragged on a 3000 gt vr-4.  It's cool clutch dump from 6grand and it rolled the tires over once and took off. That was cool, it was pretty fast yeah, nothing to get excited over, handled awesome, but man did the brakes suck!  When it came time to slow that 4500lb tank down from 130mph it was scary.  I took temp readings of the rotors after that about 3 mins, with a infra-red thermometer and it was still off the chart, over 600degrees.  The rotors were badly warped after about a half an hour of hard driving. And I also blew the 2nd gear synchonizer out.  5 grand for a new tranny. Rotors and tranny were under warranty so it's all good. but that didn't impress me especially for such a high dollar car.<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Xtreme Fiero's||10-04-2000||08:16 AM||||Hypnotise: There Is a huge diffrence For a Integra GSR and a Real Type-R a Type-R can get to the mid 13's easyly. Is that integra gsr you spoke of Yellow W/ a wings west bodykit? lives behind 40W? beacuse that is a nice car same for his buddy w/ the white 00' eclipse. Iv'e raced the Eclipse b-4 he beat my by half a car length.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000018||JohnnyK||10-04-2000||04:18 PM||||Man, I just got into this conversation today. An import car with a 2.5 will beat an american car with a 2.5 because AMERICANS CAN'T MAKE ENGINES.. I'm sure they can, but they just won't.. I don't know why..||||reg||1
Z||000019||Will||10-04-2000||04:43 PM||||JohnnyK:<BR>     Americans can make engines (LS1, Northstar, LT5, etc). They just realize that a &lt;2.0 litre 4 cylinder engine is an economy engine and don't bother wringing performance out of it.<P>Xtreme Fiero's:<BR>     The Integra Type R is a beast of a different color. Compare it to the Cobra-R mustang. Just because the Cobra-R is fast, are all mustangs fast? For crying out loud, put a Fiero up against cars in its class: Miata, MR2, 1 or 2 gen RX7 (not 3rd), Celica, regular Integra, etc.<BR>How much was the most expensive Fiero new? How much was a VR4 or 300ZX TT new?<P>To no one in particular, I just have to rant:<P>100 HP/litre is nothing special. Anything that spins past 8K rpm can make 100HP/Litre. I can squeeze 100 hp/litre out of an 8500 RPM BBC. The new race HEMI (500 CI)? 1275 HP at 8750 RPM. That's 155 HP/litre.<BR>     You wouldn't want to drive such an engine on the street, however. It would be so cammed up it wouldn't idle, it would be gutless and inefficient at low RPM, with very peaky, non-linear power delivery.<BR>     VTEC does not allow specific outputs that would not otherwise be reachable, it allows such radical engines to be tractible enough to drive on the street.<BR>     Personally, I like Toyota's VVT-i and BMW's double VANOS (systems that alter lobe separation) better than VTEC. VVT-i and double VANOS enhance low RPM driveability and increase mid-range torque, which is Honda's notorius weakness.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Will||10-04-2000||04:44 PM||||No, a Quad 4 sticker will not make your car a ricer, because that's what it actually has. Your car should be the antithesis of a ricer, because it has mods that actually INCREASE performance.||||reg||1
Z||000021||Pontiaddict||10-04-2000||04:46 PM||||When you have to build small fuel efficient cars in order to keep your car company afloat. (Like the import comanies do) You learn alot about tuning small motors for horsepower. In America, that hasn't been the case. So we build big cars with lots of torque. Although most of the bigger cars make more hp than the foreign counterpart. They aren't as efficient at making power because they don't need to be. It's alot easier to get 20 hp out of a v8 than a 4 cyl because the 4's are already more finely tuned. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||1FST2M6||10-04-2000||05:06 PM||||i see and drive the "ricer" cars almost every that i'm at the shop.. turbo civic, s/c integra.. my SE ran a 14.7 on dot slicks with NO NITROUS. a s/c civic will run 15.1! yeah its 1.5 seconds faster than stock but thats still weak. with prober tuning our 2.8s will SCREAM! with a tiny 40 shot of nitrous 13.6.. that 10psi s/c or turo territory for the ricer next to you... <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  we have low end torque.. and LOTS of it.. somthing a civic will never have... the s/c type r only lays down with an undrivable timing avance and water injection 215 at the wheels with a psi jackson racing s/c. they are great cars to drive but the severe lack of torque makes them a pain to drive in traffic but great on a slalom coarse. not as big a pain as my car was (solid clutch) but still not as civilized as a GS-R. which with intake, header and cat back will only lay down 160-170... thats not that far from a stock fiero... my and Shaun41178s dyno numbers show that.. yeah their sweet looking and tach to 9500 and everyone makes parts for them but then not so sweet as i'd got buy one. the 300zx (i trashed a 94TT and bought my se with the insurance money) it was fun but insurance was STOOPID high (i'm 23) and part were high only nissan or stillen. and 300gt.. the motors don't last very long in them... the ring were capily made and fail after about 85-90k under decent boosted driving (VR-4) the SLs aren't anything more then a sporty lookin diamante... sorry for the rant. dive these cars and tune a fiero to it's limits and you'll see how similar we all really are. ||||reg||1
Z||000023||JohnnyK||10-04-2000||05:27 PM||||Will, as you were saying, put the Fiero in it's class against the foreign cars.. Unfortunatly, every car you mentioned will beat the Fiero...||||reg||1
Z||000024||Xtreme Fiero's||10-04-2000||09:45 PM||||<BR>Pontiaddict: so you are saying that Dodge/Mitsu., Chevy/isuzu and Ford/Mazda dont need cars like the neon(eclipse powered), sunbird/Caviler or the Probe & escort (both powerd by mazda) to stay in busniess? and that they stay around for the sole purpose of makeing C5 Vetts, Vipers & FR500's?  There is no need to bad mouth a car because it's driver is a fool.<P>The 300ZX, 3000GT, RX-7, MR-2, Supra and soon the Camaro/Firebird even the Impalla 454 SS, Nova, Buick GTX and all the factory HEMI powered Mopars all died because there was no market for them any more. soon will be the fate of the Vette, Viper & Mustang. The only way to stay alive in the car market is to adapt, all of the last great imports didn't. The eclipse was the lateist to do this the 95-99' eclipse sucked unless you spent $13,000 more and got a turbo model, the same works for the Mustang & FR500. Honda has the great ability to adapt. and the suport of the largest aftermarket of any other car company in the world. the mustang is not for sale in Japan any more there is no market for it same for the Viper over there. Sports cars don't make money, compact peopple/stuf movers do.<P><BR>PS but the owner of the VTEC Civic saying that he had 30 more HP he ment the VTEC 1.6 makes 30 more HP than the SOHC 1.8  ||||reg||1
Z||000025||Xtreme Fiero's||10-04-2000||10:12 PM||||<BR>Will: the VTEC system makes the car streetable. If you where to run the "B" cam from a VTEC in a SOHC engine the car would not idle at all and miss badly below 2500rpm and the "A" cam would run out of ass buy 3500rpm. sound alot like your 500ci Hemi? but streetable and will fit in the avrage car. <P>VTEC is the single greatest advance in automotive tecnolgy, alowing you to run a truly WILD cam and still get good gass mileage.||||reg||1
Z||000026||HYPTNOTiSE||10-05-2000||03:27 AM||||No i'm not talking about the crappy integra LS with the school bus yellow body kit on it, (thats not wings west by the way, it's an offbrand cheap ****  kit) with the maaco paint job. That car sucks. only thing nice are the volk racing wheels. I've talked to that kid a bunch of times. That thing is really slow. His buddy was running 15.8's at 75-80 in the white eclpise. I'm talking about my buddy brian harts car, he's got rims and a body kit his cars teal. He works at GS communications with my buddy scott who has the 13.20 1/4 mile all motor neon. My other buddy's who have integras are bengie and this guy sam from down the road.  Sam has an 8 pound jackson and his cars slow cos he can't drive. So far bengie's fastest time is a 14.0 on slicks. And bengie is one of the best drivers i know.  His car is dark green with 17'' rims and lowered. He just blew his engine not too long ago, and my buddy chris with a black GSR is considering buying his blower.  Bengie's ****  blew because he didn't have an upgraded fuel pump, whoops, detonation in 3rd gear at 7900rpm sure will kill an engine.  And as far as the difference between a type-r and a GSR it's not a huge difference. I wouldn't call 20hp a huge difference.  I know of one for sale right now. it's white and has a turbo and stuff, supposed to be damn fast. he said he payed 24 for it new and invested 18grand and he's selling it for 18,500.<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||Eric_PA||10-05-2000||09:42 AM||||Thanks so far for the feedback. I am allready on my way to performing this swap, but decided to see where I would stand with this. I just want something different and figure this is the way. I allready have a moded 97 Sunfire GT that can run 15.5 in the Quarter. This car is the reason I decided to go with a Quad swap. As far as American 4 cylinder engines, I think that the domestic companies are finally waking up. I think that the Sunfire GT/Cav Z-24 and Escort ZX2 along with the Neon RT are good examples. Time will tell if the reliability is there, but I think they are headed in the right direction.<P>Eric<BR>86.5 Black GT---&gt; Quad GT<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000028||whamel||10-05-2000||09:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Will, as you were saying, put the Fiero in it's class against the foreign cars.. Unfortunatly, every car you mentioned will beat the Fiero...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I can at least vouch for the Integra - my '87 Integra LS would pretty much beat my '88 Iron Duke Fiero all around.  It's lighter, handles better (stock), and has more HP (slightly less torque).  And that's with no mods at all - straight as the factory put it together.  Oh yeah, it gets better highway gas mileage too on top of it all.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I still love my Fiero's though!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000029||DaRkLoRD||10-05-2000||10:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by whamel:<BR><B> <BR>I can at least vouch for the Integra - my '87 Integra LS would pretty much beat my '88 Iron Duke Fiero all around.  It's lighter, handles better (stock), and has more HP (slightly less torque).  And that's with no mods at all - straight as the factory put it together.  Oh yeah, it gets better highway gas mileage too on top of it all.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I still love my Fiero's though!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't think it's too hard to beat a duke..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000030||Standard||10-05-2000||01:05 PM||||I always beat my ex's '90 Celica 5 speed in my 84 auto.  It's not because she can't drive, she's been driving a stick since she had her first car, but it's because the duke has more torque!  IMO torque rules, and there's no way you can get a decent amount of torque out of a small-displacement 4 banger.  Look at the Honda S-2000.. sure it has almost twice the hp of our v6's, but if you want any kind of decent launch you have to rev it to 6 grand.... anyways, a nice deep-throated growl sounds better than a high-pitched buzzing.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 151,000 miles and counting!        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">     <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000031||ChadMan||10-05-2000||01:33 PM||||Why did GM give up on the H.O. Quad 4?  160-190 hp from 2.3 liters is pretty impressive.  I know they blew head gaskets, but couldn't GM have solved that problem?  I have to believe with the brains and money GM has, it could match Honda for output AND reliability if it really tried.<P>The 2.4 Twin Cam (Quad 4, part II) might make a good swap, but it trades hp for torque - meaning you might as well go with a 2.8 V6.  I mean, high revs and high HP is the whole point of a DOHC 4-banger.  Why wouldn't GM make a high-output version of the 2.4?  I'd have to think 200 hp wouldn't be out of the question.||||reg||5
Z||000032||whamel||10-05-2000||03:30 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B>  IMO torque rules, and there's no way you can get a decent amount of torque out of a small-displacement 4 banger.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yeah 244 hp and 217 ft/torque isn't a whole heck of a lot out of a 2.2 Litre engine, is it?  I think they could have done better! <BR><p>[This message has been edited by whamel (edited 10-05-2000).]||||reg||1
