Z||000036||Formula 18||10-05-2000||09:58 PM||||Interusting thread. A kid I grew up with Is buying a Honda Prelude and is gonna Rice it up. System, windsheild banners, the whole works. It looks ok but I would never drive it. My uncle has a 92 Prelude with 4 wheel steering and that thing coners. <P>It's an auto and I was really impressed by how it got off the line though. It is quick but 12,000 worth of quick. <P>In my Opion HP will sell cars but torque will win races off the line. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Brian<BR> -88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000037||Will||10-05-2000||10:17 PM||||Xtreme:<BR>     Did you even read what I wrote about VTEC? Go back and read it again for the first time.<P>JohnnyK:<BR>     Beat a Fiero in what?<BR>     A first gen RX7 with solid rear axle, pizza cutter tires on 13" wheels and rear drums isn't much competition.<BR>     The N/A 1st Gen MR2's aren't even close. (So few S/Ced that I won't mention them) The 2nd gen gained so much weight that the extra power is almost cancelled out. The new MR2 might be a different story.<BR>     Of the Celicas, only the NEW GTS is competition.<BR>     Regular Integras run on puny 185 tires. GSR's are fast, but still don't have enough tire.<BR>     Miata's, while not that fast, do handle very well, and seem to do well in AutoX with competent drivers.<BR>     Don't forget that while some of these cars post impressive HP numbers, NONE of them can even come close to the Fiero's 175 ft-lbs of torque.<P>Pontiaddict:<BR>     It's easier to get 20 HP out of a V8 than a 4 cylinder because the V8 has 2-4 times the displacement of the 4 cylinder, in addition to generally being in a lower state of tune. V8's are also easily upgraded to states of tune similar to import engines.<BR>     Cars w/ 400+ RWHP, while not everywhere, are not uncommon at the forum at <A HREF="http://www.ls1.com." TARGET=_blank>www.ls1.com.</A> <P><BR>If anyone thinks that GM can't build a 4 banger, look at the SD4.<BR>     I'd like to build a Fiero with an aluminum block (do they make these?) SD4 running about 30 psi of boost. That would be a ride.<BR>||||reg||1
